From: PA-220 port
Subject: watchdog: octeon-wdt: report the real timeout

octeon_wdt_set_timeout() never updates wdd->timeout, and the device is
registered with the hardware interrupt period (5 s on a CN7130) as its
timeout instead of the heartbeat. WDIOC_SETTIMEOUT returns wdd->timeout,
so procd asks for 30 s, reads back 5, and uses 5 the next time it sets
the timeout: countdown_reset becomes 0 and a userspace stall of ~10 s
already ends in the NMI stage. Report the heartbeat instead.
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/octeon-wdt-main.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/octeon-wdt-main.c
@@ -462,6 +462,12 @@
 		return -1;
 
 	octeon_wdt_calc_parameters(t);
+	/*
+	 * The watchdog core reports wdd->timeout back to WDIOC_SETTIMEOUT.
+	 * Left at the 5 s interrupt period, procd reads 5 back and uses it
+	 * for its next SETTIMEOUT, shrinking the real timeout to ~10 s.
+	 */
+	wdog->timeout = heartbeat;
 
 	if (disable)
 		return 0;
@@ -555,7 +561,7 @@
 
 	pr_info("Initial granularity %d Sec\n", timeout_sec);
 
-	octeon_wdt.timeout	= timeout_sec;
+	octeon_wdt.timeout	= heartbeat;
 	octeon_wdt.max_timeout	= UINT_MAX;
 
 	watchdog_set_nowayout(&octeon_wdt, nowayout);
